### `public-auth` vs profile (current)

| Route | Purpose today | Status |
| ----- | ------------- | ------ |
| `POST /api/public-auth/phone-preflight` | OTP preflight | KEEP |
| `POST /api/public-auth/request-otp` | OTP issue | KEEP |
| `POST /api/public-auth/verify-otp` | OTP verify + cookie | KEEP |
| `POST /api/public-auth/register-complete` | Onboarding profile | KEEP (onboarding only) |
| `GET/PATCH /api/public-auth/session-profile` | Legacy profile BFF | **REMOVED M4** — use `/api/me/profile` |

### Session handling (actual)

1. `verify-otp` / `register-complete` BFF sets `atour_mb_session` via `setSessionCookieOnResponse`.
2. `readPublicCatalogSessionFromCookies` decodes JWT; accepts `owner | admin | member | viewer`.
3. `buildMemberApiHeaders` adds `Authorization: Bearer` + `x-user-id` + `x-actor-role` for member BFF calls.
4. `me/profile/page.tsx` uses `fetchMemberProfile()` → same-origin `GET /api/me/profile` only.

